- Open-Meteo historical weather (ERA5), historical forecast (NOAA GFS, pressure levels) and marine
  APIs <https://open-meteo.com/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- LOM_SITE.rock.d, LOM_TRACED[].globe, LOM_FAN: distances are great circles on a 6,371 km sphere
  from coordinates (the camera located on Copernicus GLO-30), and the globe's rays are traced over
  that sphere
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): The horizon where the photograph puts it on the rock,
  given by rays traced over a plane in air the model and the reanalysis allow, while the globe needs
  implausible air.
